window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-dea5d8982f047a3a"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"plugins\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">插件</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。如需查看文档的 Markdown 版本，可在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"overview\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">概览</h2> <p>插件将多种能力打包为可在 ChatGPT 和 Codex 中重复使用的工作流程。插件可以包含技能（Skills）和 MCP 服务器。两款产品使用同一个通用插件目录，因此可以在各自支持的界面中发现相同的公开插件。</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pKwRNdDtai0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">观看：ChatGPT 中的插件（需联网）</a></p> <p>在网页、桌面和移动端的 ChatGPT 中，插件可用于 Chat 和 Work；在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中，插件也可用于 Codex。Codex CLI 还提供插件浏览器，供 Codex 环境使用。IDE 扩展不支持插件。</p> <p>在移动端，你可以在 Chat 或 Work 中使用账户可用的插件。</p> <p><strong>工作区管理员请注意：</strong>请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1\">工作区连接</a>，以配置由公司管理的应用账户，并控制哪些人可以使用这些账户。身份验证方式决定请求使用哪个外部身份及其权限。</p> <p>标记为<strong>仅限桌面端</strong>的插件需要使用 ChatGPT 桌面应用。你可以在网页上找到这些插件，但必须打开 ChatGPT 桌面应用才能安装和使用；移动端无法使用这些插件。</p> <p>如需了解插件的安装和使用方法，请参阅帮助中心的<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001256\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT 和 Codex 中的插件（需联网）</a>。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>打开 <strong>Plugins（插件）</strong>标签页来浏览和安装插件。安装后，你可以在 ChatGPT 的 Chat 或 Work 中，或者在 Codex 中使用插件。已安装的插件可以为新聊天添加技能和 MCP 工具。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>打开 <strong>Plugins（插件）</strong>标签页来浏览和安装插件。安装后，你可以在 Chat 或 Work 中使用插件。插件可能会要求你先连接外部服务，然后才开放其工具。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在 Codex CLI 中输入 <code>/plugins</code> 打开插件浏览器。从已配置的市场安装插件后，先启动新会话，再使用其中附带的技能或工具。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"plugin-directory-in-the-ide-extension\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"use-plugins-from-a-supported-surface\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">在受支持的平台中使用插件</h3> <p>IDE 扩展中没有插件功能。若要为 Codex 浏览和安装插件，请使用 ChatGPT 桌面应用或 Codex CLI。</p> <p>插件可以扩展 ChatGPT 和 Codex 的能力，例如：</p> <ul> <li>安装 Codex Security 插件，扫描已获授权的代码，并确认可信的漏洞发现结果。</li> <li>安装 Gmail 插件，以便使用 Gmail。</li> <li>安装 Google Drive 插件，以便使用 Drive、Docs、Sheets 和 Slides。</li> <li>安装 Slack 插件，以便总结频道内容或起草回复。</li> </ul> <p>插件可以包含以下一个或多个部分：</p> <ul> <li><strong>技能（Skills）：</strong>针对特定工作类型的可复用指令。ChatGPT 和 Codex 可在需要时加载这些指令，以便按正确步骤执行任务并使用适当的参考资料或辅助脚本。</li> <li><strong>MCP 服务器：</strong>将 ChatGPT 和 Codex 连接到 GitHub、Slack 或 Google Drive 等系统中的工具和信息的服务。它们定义工具、执行身份验证、返回结构化数据，并对外部系统执行操作；也可以选择包含自定义界面。</li> <li><strong>浏览器扩展：</strong>插件工作流程所需的浏览器能力。</li> <li><strong>钩子（Hooks）：</strong>在 Codex 运行时配置的生命周期节点执行的命令。由云端编排的 ChatGPT Work 不支持插件钩子。同步版 Work 仅支持在 Agent Security 中配置的管理员定义 MCP 钩子；请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad?anchor=check-compatibility-and-data-requirements\">Work 线程同步兼容性</a>。钩子脚本必须在执行环境中可用；在网页上安装插件不会部署这些脚本。企业管理员可以通过移动设备管理（MDM）部署所需脚本。运行前请检查并信任插件钩子。有关设置和托管钩子策略，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-0aecdb1ef0cec0a4\">Hooks</a>。</li> </ul> <p>你可以通过市场来源发布插件来共享，例如为项目或团队创建代码仓库市场。有关市场设置、打包和分发说明，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">构建插件</a>。</p> <p>如果你正在构建集成，请从<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/mcp-server.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">构建 MCP 服务器</a>开始。如果插件需要自定义界面，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/chatgpt-ui.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">可选界面指南</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"use-and-install-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">使用和安装插件</h2> <p><a id=\"plugin-directory-in-the-codex-app\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"universal-plugin-directory\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">通用插件目录</h3> <p>ChatGPT 和 Codex 使用同一个公开插件目录。在网页或 ChatGPT 桌面应用中，打开 <strong>Plugins（插件）</strong>标签页即可浏览和安装插件。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>插件目录按标签页对插件进行分类：</p> <ul> <li><strong>OpenAI：</strong>由 OpenAI 构建的插件。</li> <li><strong>你的工作区名称：</strong>由工作区提供的插件。</li> <li><strong>Personal（个人）：</strong>个人市场中的插件；如果有可用插件，还会包含 <strong>Created by me（由我创建）</strong>和 <strong>Shared with me（与我共享）</strong>分区。</li> </ul> <p>使用单独的 <strong>Installed（已安装）</strong>行查看你已安装的插件。</p> <p>工作区管理员可以为团队导入并同步 GitHub 市场。有关设置和访问要求，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-ab115ea47731f92a\">插件管理</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"install-and-use-a-plugin\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">安装和使用插件</h3> <p>打开插件目录后：</p> <ol> <li>搜索或浏览插件，然后打开其详情。</li> <li>选择加号按钮安装插件。</li> <li>如果插件需要连接 MCP 服务器，请按提示完成连接。有些插件会在安装时要求你进行身份验证；另一些则会等到你首次使用时再要求验证。</li> <li>安装完成后，启动新聊天，并让 ChatGPT 或 Codex 使用该插件。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"connect-supported-partners-with-sign-in-with-chatgpt\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"sign-in-with-chatgpt\">使用 Sign in with ChatGPT 连接受支持的合作伙伴</h3> <p><strong>Sign in with ChatGPT</strong> 正在面向受支持的插件和合作伙伴网站逐步推出测试版，包括 Airtable、GitLab、HubSpot、Notion、Supabase 和 Vercel。如果看到此选项，在连接插件时选择 <strong>Sign in with ChatGPT</strong>，即可为该服务创建账户或关联现有账户。</p> <p>登录时仅会与合作伙伴共享你的姓名、电子邮件地址和（如果有）个人资料图片。此操作不会授予插件访问你数据的权限，也不会自动批准任何操作。使用连接前，请另行检查并批准插件请求的权限。</p> <p>安装插件后，你可以直接在提示窗口中使用它：</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"describe-the-task-directly\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_7\">直接描述任务</h4> <p>描述你想要的结果，例如“总结今天尚未阅读的 Gmail 线程”或“从 Google Drive 获取最新发布说明”。</p> <p>如果希望 ChatGPT 为任务选择合适的已安装工具，请使用这种方式。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-specific-plugin\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_8\">指定某个插件</h4> <p>输入 <code>@</code>，即可明确调用插件或其中包含的技能。</p> <p>如果希望明确指定 ChatGPT 应使用哪个插件或技能，请使用这种方式。另请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-f06621b97709dae2\">技能与插件</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"bring-your-own-plugins-in-sites\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"plugins-in-sites\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"sites\">在 Sites 中使用插件</h3> <p>在 Sites 中使用插件，可以构建一个使用每位访问者自己的已连接账户和权限的网站。设置方法和访问者访问要求，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-e0f092cc982945c2?anchor=bring-user-data-to-your-site-with-plugins\">通过插件将用户数据接入 Site</a>。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"use-apple-messages-from-codex\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex-apple-messages\">在 Codex 中使用 Apple Messages</h3> <p>Apple Messages 插件适用于 macOS 版 ChatGPT 桌面应用的所有套餐。在 Codex 和 ChatGPT Work 中，它可以读取和搜索 Mac 上的 iMessage、SMS 和 RCS 对话，并通过“信息”应用代你发送消息。它不能让你通过“信息”远程与 ChatGPT 交互，也不能用于普通的 ChatGPT 聊天。</p> <p>在此版本中，“信息”插件仅包含在 Apple Silicon（arm64）版 ChatGPT 桌面应用中。</p> <ol> <li>打开 <strong>Plugins（插件）</strong>，找到 Apple Messages 插件并安装。</li> <li>新建 Codex 或 ChatGPT Work 聊天，然后让它查找、总结、起草或发送消息。</li> <li>在 ChatGPT 读取“信息”之前，授予它所请求的 macOS 权限。</li> <li>允许发送前，检查消息内容及收件人。</li> </ol> <p>默认情况下，ChatGPT 只有在你批准消息内容和收件人后才会发送。选择 <strong>Allow once（允许一次）</strong>，仅批准本次发送。如果选择 <strong>Always allow sending to this chat（始终允许向此聊天发送）</strong>，ChatGPT 今后可以向该“信息”聊天发送消息，而无需再次取得发送批准。</p> <p>对于可能包含不可信或误导性指令的聊天，请保留逐条发送审批。持续授权会取消 ChatGPT 代你发送消息前最后一次审核机会。只有在你接受这一风险时才使用此选项。</p> <p>若要恢复逐条发送审批，请打开 <strong>Settings（设置）</strong> &gt; <strong>Computer use（电脑操作）</strong>，然后选择 <strong>Messages（信息）</strong>旁边的 <strong>Manage（管理）</strong>。在 <strong>Always allowed to send（始终允许发送）</strong>下，选择该聊天旁的垃圾桶图标，然后确认 <strong>Remove（移除）</strong>。之后，ChatGPT 每次向该聊天发送消息前都会再次询问。</p> <p><strong>已知问题：</strong>如果任务设置为 <strong>Full access（完全访问）</strong>，或以其他方式关闭了审批提示，Apple Messages 可能无法显示发送所需的确认窗口。请切换到 <strong>Ask for approval（请求批准）</strong>或 <strong>Approve for me（代我批准）</strong>后重试。</p> <p>Apple Messages 在你的 Mac 上运行，无法直接用于网页版或移动版 ChatGPT、Codex CLI 或 IDE 扩展。</p> <p>在受管理的工作区中，管理员可以通过现有的 Computer Use 控制项停用 Apple Messages。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"plugin-directory-in-codex-cli\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"plugin-browser-in-codex-cli\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex-cli\">Codex CLI 中的插件浏览器</h3> <p>在 Codex CLI 中运行以下命令即可打开插件浏览器：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">codex\n/plugins\n</code></pre> <p>CLI 插件浏览器按市场对插件分组。使用市场标签页切换来源，打开插件查看详情，安装或卸载市场条目；选中已安装的插件后，按 <kbd>Space</kbd> 键即可启用或停用它。</p> <p><a id=\"api-key-availability\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"api\">API 密钥的可用性</h3> <p>如果你<a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115?anchor=sign-in-with-an-api-key\">使用 OpenAI API 密钥登录 Codex</a>，便可以在 Codex CLI 和 ChatGPT 桌面应用中的 Codex 浏览、安装和管理受支持的 OpenAI 精选插件。由于部分插件的连接流程需要当前不支持的 OAuth 功能，因此无法通过 API 密钥身份验证使用。请在 <a href=\"https://platform.openai.com/usage\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Platform Usage 页面（需联网）</a>查看插件用量。</p> <p><a id=\"how-permissions-and-data-sharing-work\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">权限和数据共享的工作方式</h3> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在网页版 ChatGPT 中，Chat 和 Work 使用该聊天可用的工作区权限与工具。MCP 服务器仍需要获得授权并访问已连接的服务。个人连接使用你自己的账户；在受支持的体验中，可以重复使用已授权的共享账户连接，无需每次输入该账户的凭据。部分方法还要求请求者通过验证。请检查连接将使用哪个身份。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>当插件功能通过 Codex 主机运行时，适用该主机的<a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">沙盒和审批策略</a>。连接外部服务时，则使用该服务自身的身份验证和访问控制。</p> <ul> <li>安装后，新建聊天或 CLI 会话时即可使用插件中包含的技能。</li> <li>如果插件包含 MCP 服务器，使用前可能需要额外设置或身份验证。</li> <li>ChatGPT 通过 MCP 服务器发送数据时，适用该服务的条款和隐私政策。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"remove-a-plugin\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">移除插件</h3> <p>若要移除插件，请在受支持的插件浏览器中打开该插件；如果提供此操作，请选择 <strong>Uninstall plugin（卸载插件）</strong>。通过工作区安装的插件或默认插件可能不提供此操作，而是由工作区管理员统一管理。</p> <p>卸载插件会从相应的 ChatGPT 或 Codex 环境中移除该插件包。单独连接的 MCP 服务器集成仍会在 ChatGPT 中保持连接，直到你在 ChatGPT 中将其断开。</p> <p><a id=\"build-your-own-plugin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">构建自己的插件</h2> <p>若要通过 ChatGPT 对话创建或编辑插件，请从<a href=\"#/article/a-0d81218eacd2463c\">构建插件</a>开始。当你的工作区提供 Plugin Creator 时，本指南将带你描述工作流程、添加参考文件、测试插件并修改内容。</p> <p>若要创建、测试或分发自己的插件，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件构建开发者指南</a>。该指南介绍本地脚手架、手动设置市场、工作区共享、插件清单和打包方法。</p> <p>如果插件包含由服务器提供的功能，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/mcp-server.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">构建 MCP 服务器</a>。MCP 工具可以不使用自定义界面，也可以在界面有助于工作流程时返回界面。</p> <p>插件准备好接受审核后，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/deploy/submission.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">提交插件</a>，了解 OpenAI Platform 的提交流程、所需权限、审核材料、MCP 检查和测试用例要求。</p> <p><a id=\"plugin-guides\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_12\">插件指南</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-2c6e218368c091d9\">录制与回放</a>：向 ChatGPT 演示一次工作流程，并将其转化为可重复使用的技能。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-bec1e26cb654a758\">Codex Security 插件</a>：扫描已获授权的代码、确认发现的问题，并准备经过审核的修复方案。</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"plugins\">Plugins</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"overview\">Overview</h2> <p>Plugins bundle capabilities into reusable workflows in ChatGPT and Codex. They can include skills and MCP servers. Both products use one universal plugin directory, so the same public plugins are discoverable from their supported surfaces.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pKwRNdDtai0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Watch: Plugins in ChatGPT (online)</a></p> <p>Plugins work in Chat and Work across ChatGPT on the web, desktop, and mobile, and in Codex in the ChatGPT desktop app. Codex CLI also has a plugin browser for Codex environments. The IDE extension doesn't support plugins.</p> <p>On mobile, you can use plugins available to your account in Chat or Work.</p> <p><strong>For workspace admins:</strong> See <a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1\">Workspace connections</a> to configure company-managed app accounts and control who can use them. The authentication method determines which external identity and permissions a request uses.</p> <p>Plugins marked <strong>Desktop only</strong> require the ChatGPT desktop app. You can discover these plugins on the web, but you must open the ChatGPT desktop app to install and use them. They aren't available on mobile.</p> <p>For help installing and using plugins, see <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001256\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Plugins in ChatGPT and Codex (online)</a> in the Help Center.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Open the <strong>Plugins</strong> tab to browse and install plugins. After installation, you can use plugins in Chat or Work in ChatGPT, or in Codex. Installed plugins can add skills and MCP tools to new chats.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Open the <strong>Plugins</strong> tab to browse and install plugins. After installation, you can use plugins in Chat or Work. A plugin can prompt you to connect an external service before its tools become available.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>In Codex CLI, enter <code>/plugins</code> to open the plugin browser. Install a plugin from a configured marketplace, then start a new session before using its bundled skills or tools.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"plugin-directory-in-the-ide-extension\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"use-plugins-from-a-supported-surface\">Use plugins from a supported surface</h3> <p>Plugins aren't available in the IDE extension. To browse and install plugins for Codex, use the ChatGPT desktop app or Codex CLI.</p> <p>Extend what ChatGPT and Codex can do, for example:</p> <ul> <li>Install the Codex Security plugin to scan authorized code and confirm plausible vulnerability findings.</li> <li>Install the Gmail plugin to work with Gmail.</li> <li>Install the Google Drive plugin to work across Drive, Docs, Sheets, and Slides.</li> <li>Install the Slack plugin to summarize channels or draft replies.</li> </ul> <p>A plugin can contain one or more of these parts:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Skills:</strong> reusable instructions for specific kinds of work. ChatGPT and Codex can load them when needed so they follow the right steps and use the right references or helper scripts for a task.</li> <li><strong>MCP servers:</strong> services that connect ChatGPT and Codex to tools and information in systems such as GitHub, Slack, or Google Drive. They define tools, enforce authentication, return structured data, and perform actions against external systems. They can optionally include custom UI.</li> <li><strong>Browser extensions:</strong> browser capabilities that a plugin needs for its workflow.</li> <li><strong>Hooks:</strong> commands that run at configured lifecycle points in the Codex runtime. Plugin hooks are not supported in cloud-orchestrated ChatGPT Work. Synced Work supports only admin-defined MCP hooks configured in Agent Security; see <a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad?anchor=check-compatibility-and-data-requirements\">Work thread sync compatibility</a>. Hook scripts must be available in the execution environment; installing a plugin on the web doesn't deploy those scripts. Enterprise admins can deploy required scripts through mobile device management (MDM). Review and trust plugin hooks before they run. See <a href=\"#/article/a-0aecdb1ef0cec0a4\">Hooks</a> for setup and managed-hook policies.</li> </ul> <p>You can share plugins by publishing them through a marketplace source, such as a repo marketplace for a project or team. See <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build plugins</a> for marketplace setup, packaging, and distribution guidance.</p> <p>If you are building an integration, start with <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/mcp-server.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build an MCP server</a>. If the plugin needs custom UI, use the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/chatgpt-ui.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">optional UI guide</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"use-and-install-plugins\">Use and install plugins</h2> <p><a id=\"plugin-directory-in-the-codex-app\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,web</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"universal-plugin-directory\">Universal plugin directory</h3> <p>ChatGPT and Codex use the same public plugin catalog. On the web or in the ChatGPT desktop app, open the <strong>Plugins</strong> tab to browse and install plugins.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>The Plugins Directory organizes plugins into tabs:</p> <ul> <li><strong>OpenAI:</strong> plugins built by OpenAI.</li> <li><strong>Your workspace name:</strong> plugins provided by your workspace.</li> <li><strong>Personal:</strong> personal marketplace plugins, including <strong>Created by me</strong> and <strong>Shared with me</strong> sections when those plugins are available.</li> </ul> <p>Use the separate <strong>Installed</strong> row to review plugins you already installed.</p> <p>Workspace admins can import and sync a GitHub marketplace for their team. See <a href=\"#/article/a-ab115ea47731f92a\">Plugin management</a> for setup and access requirements.</p> <h3 id=\"install-and-use-a-plugin\">Install and use a plugin</h3> <p>Once you open the Plugins Directory:</p> <ol> <li>Search or browse for a plugin, then open its details.</li> <li>Select the plus button to install the plugin.</li> <li>If the plugin needs an MCP server connection, connect it when prompted. Some plugins ask you to authenticate during install. Others wait until the first time you use them.</li> <li>After installation, start a new chat and ask ChatGPT or Codex to use the plugin.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"connect-supported-partners-with-sign-in-with-chatgpt\">Connect supported partners with Sign in with ChatGPT</h3> <p><strong>Sign in with ChatGPT</strong> is rolling out in beta for supported plugins and partner sites, including Airtable, GitLab, HubSpot, Notion, Supabase, and Vercel. When the option is available, select <strong>Sign in with ChatGPT</strong> while connecting the plugin to create or link your account with that service.</p> <p>Signing in shares only your name, email address, and profile picture, when available, with the partner. It doesn't grant the plugin access to your data or approve actions automatically. Review and approve the plugin's requested permissions as a separate step before using the connection.</p> <p>After you install a plugin, you can use it directly in the prompt window:</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,web</strong></p> </blockquote> <h4 id=\"describe-the-task-directly\">Describe the task directly</h4> <p>Ask for the outcome you want, such as \"Summarize unread Gmail threads from today\" or \"Pull the latest launch notes from Google Drive.\"</p> <p>Use this when you want ChatGPT to choose the right installed tools for the task.</p> <h4 id=\"choose-a-specific-plugin\">Choose a specific plugin</h4> <p>Type <code>@</code> to invoke the plugin or one of its bundled skills explicitly.</p> <p>Use this when you want to be specific about which plugin or skill ChatGPT should use. See <a href=\"#/article/a-f06621b97709dae2\">Skills &amp; Plugins</a>.</p> <p><a id=\"bring-your-own-plugins-in-sites\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"plugins-in-sites\">Plugins in Sites</h3> <p>Use plugins in Sites to build a Site that uses each visitor's own connected accounts and permissions. See <a href=\"#/article/a-e0f092cc982945c2?anchor=bring-user-data-to-your-site-with-plugins\">Bring user data to your Site with plugins</a> for setup and visitor access requirements.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"use-apple-messages-from-codex\">Use Apple Messages from Codex</h3> <p>The Apple Messages plugin is available on all plans in the ChatGPT desktop app for macOS. In Codex and ChatGPT Work, it can read and search iMessage, SMS, and RCS chats on your Mac and send messages on your behalf through the Messages app. It doesn't let you interact with ChatGPT remotely through Messages, and it doesn't work in regular ChatGPT chats.</p> <p>For this release, the Messages plugin is included only in the Apple Silicon (arm64) build of the ChatGPT desktop app.</p> <ol> <li>Open <strong>Plugins</strong>, find the Apple Messages plugin, and install it.</li> <li>Start a new Codex or ChatGPT Work chat and ask it to find, summarize, draft, or send a message.</li> <li>Grant the requested macOS permissions before ChatGPT reads Messages.</li> <li>Review the message and its recipients before allowing a send.</li> </ol> <p>By default, ChatGPT sends messages only after you approve the message and its recipients. Choose <strong>Allow once</strong> to approve only that send. If you select <strong>Always allow sending to this chat</strong>, ChatGPT can send future messages to that Messages chat without another send approval.</p> <p>Keep per-send approval for chats that may contain untrusted or misleading instructions. Persistent approval removes your final chance to review a message before ChatGPT sends it as you. Use it only when you accept that risk.</p> <p>To restore per-send approval, open <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Computer use</strong> and select <strong>Manage</strong> next to <strong>Messages</strong>. Under <strong>Always allowed to send</strong>, select the trash icon next to the chat, then confirm <strong>Remove</strong>. ChatGPT will ask before sending to that chat again.</p> <p><strong>Known issue:</strong> If your task is set to <strong>Full access</strong> or otherwise disables approval prompts, Apple Messages may be unable to show the confirmation needed to send. Switch to <strong>Ask for approval</strong> or <strong>Approve for me</strong> and try again.</p> <p>Apple Messages runs on your Mac. It isn't directly available in ChatGPT on the web or mobile, Codex CLI, or the IDE extension.</p> <p>In managed workspaces, administrators can disable Apple Messages through the existing Computer Use control.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"plugin-directory-in-codex-cli\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"plugin-browser-in-codex-cli\">Plugin browser in Codex CLI</h3> <p>In Codex CLI, run the following command to open the plugin browser:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">codex\n/plugins\n</code></pre> <p>The CLI plugin browser groups plugins by marketplace. Use the marketplace tabs to switch sources, open a plugin to inspect details, install or uninstall marketplace entries, and press <kbd>Space</kbd> on an installed plugin to turn it on or off.</p> <p><a id=\"api-key-availability\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"api-key-availability\">API key availability</h3> <p>If you <a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115?anchor=sign-in-with-an-api-key\">sign in to Codex with an OpenAI API key</a>, you can browse, install, and manage supported OpenAI-curated plugins in Codex CLI and Codex in the ChatGPT desktop app. Some plugins aren't available with API key authentication because their connection flows require unsupported OAuth capabilities. Review plugin usage on the <a href=\"https://platform.openai.com/usage\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Platform Usage page (online)</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"how-permissions-and-data-sharing-work\">How permissions and data sharing work</h3> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>In ChatGPT on the web, Chat and Work use the workspace permissions and tools available to that chat. MCP servers still require authorization and access to the connected service. A personal connection uses your own account. A supported experience can reuse an authorized shared-account connection without requiring you to enter that account's credentials each time. Some methods also require a verified requester. Check which identity the connection will use.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>When a plugin capability runs through a Codex host, the host's <a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">sandbox and approval policy</a> applies. Connections to external services use that service's own authentication and access controls.</p> <ul> <li>Bundled skills become available when you start a new chat or CLI session after installation.</li> <li>If a plugin includes MCP servers, they may require extra setup or authentication before you can use them.</li> <li>When ChatGPT sends data through an MCP server, that service's terms and privacy policy apply.</li> </ul> <h3 id=\"remove-a-plugin\">Remove a plugin</h3> <p>To remove a plugin, open it from a supported plugin browser and select <strong>Uninstall plugin</strong> when that action is available. Workspace-installed or default plugins may not offer that action; your workspace administrator controls them instead.</p> <p>Uninstalling a plugin removes the plugin bundle from that ChatGPT or Codex environment. Separately connected MCP server integrations remain connected in ChatGPT until you disconnect them there.</p> <h2 id=\"build-your-own-plugin\">Build your own plugin</h2> <p>To create or edit a plugin through a conversation in ChatGPT, start with <a href=\"#/article/a-0d81218eacd2463c\">Build plugins</a>. The guide walks through describing a workflow, adding reference files, testing it, and making changes when Plugin Creator is available in your workspace.</p> <p>If you want to create, test, or distribute your own plugin, see <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">our developer guide on building plugins</a>. That page covers local scaffolding, manual marketplace setup, workspace sharing, plugin manifests, and packaging guidance.</p> <p>If your plugin includes server-backed capabilities, see <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/mcp-server.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build an MCP server</a>. MCP tools can work without custom UI or return UI when a visual surface helps the workflow.</p> <p>When your plugin is ready for review, see <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/deploy/submission.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Submit plugins</a> for the OpenAI Platform submission flow, required permissions, review materials, MCP checks, and test case requirements.</p> <h2 id=\"plugin-guides\">Plugin guides</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-2c6e218368c091d9\">Record &amp; Replay</a>: Show ChatGPT a workflow once and turn it into a reusable skill.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-bec1e26cb654a758\">Codex Security plugin</a>: Scan authorized code, confirm findings, and prepare reviewed fixes.</li> </ul>"};
